    "## Executive summary "
     "This project investigates two structural questions for deterministic finite automata (DFA), namely synchronisation: does there exist a single word that, no matter what state we start in, we always end up at the same state, and how such words can be found efficiently. Isomorphism: are two DFAs equivalent, to varying strengths; Strict isomorphism, weak isomorphism and semi-isomorphism- which differ according to whether initial states, accepting states and alphabet labels must be preserved.\n", 
     "\n",
      "We implement and test various algorithms for each task, comparing their behaviour on examples and supplementing suitable sections with an extension past the project specification where we found further interesting results.\n", 
     "\n",
     "Throughout this project, we place emphasis on correct mathematical definitions, justified design of each algorithm and a concise interpretation of results. 
    "\n",
   ]
